# SOUNDTRACKS, which track answers for which, when Sinnoh plays another
# cartridge's music.
#
# The `soundtrack` launcher key swaps the archive behind the game's own
# sequence ids for one composed by mmo/tools/soundtrack.py, and this file is
# the composition: one row per Platinum track, one cell per foreign game
# naming the track that replaces it. A Platinum track with no row, or no cell
# for the chosen game, keeps its own music, jingles, fanfares and sound
# effects are deliberately not here at all, because they load out of resident
# banks rather than per track, and because system sounds staying constant is
# what makes the switch read as a soundtrack and not a different game.
#
#   <platinum SEQ name>  heartgold=<SEQ name>  blackwhite=<SEQ name>
#
# Cells may come in either order and either may be absent. A name that is not
# in its game's archive stops the compose; nothing here is fuzzy-matched.
#
# THE PAIRING IS A JUDGMENT, ROW BY ROW. Same role where the role exists
# (surf for surf, wild battle for wild battle, evolution for evolution), and
# the closest neighbour where it does not (Johto has no snow route; Black has
# no Amity Square). Several Platinum tracks may share one foreign track; the
# compose carries that track once. Retuning the soundtrack is editing a cell
# and running `make -C mmo soundtrack` again.

